---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../../consts';

const updated = 'June 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — KC Chat"
  description="How KC Chat handles your data. Cards are anonymous, the extension runs locally, and your conversations stay between you and Cursor."
>
  <section class="section legal">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p class="intro">
        KC Chat is built around a simple principle: collect as little as possible. Cards are anonymous
        bearer credentials, and once your extension is activated it validates licenses locally — it does
        not phone home with your prompts or code.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Card code</strong> — to issue and validate your license token.</li>
        <li><strong>Device fingerprint (hash)</strong> — a one-way hash used to bind a card to a single machine and prevent sharing. We cannot reverse it to identify your hardware.</li>
        <li><strong>Minimal activation logs</strong> — timestamp and tier of an activation, for fraud prevention and support.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we do <em>not</em> collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your conversations, prompts, or source code — these never leave your machine through us.</li>
        <li>Your name, address, or a user account — cards require no signup.</li>
        <li>Payment card numbers — payments are handled by third-party processors, not stored by us.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies &amp; analytics</h2>
      <p>
        The marketing site uses no advertising cookies. If privacy-friendly, aggregate analytics are
        enabled, they record page views without personally identifying you.
      </p>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        Activation records are retained only as long as needed to operate licenses and prevent abuse.
        You may request deletion of records tied to your card by contacting us.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="disclaimer">
        This page is a plain-language summary provided for transparency and is not legal advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal .container { max-width: 760px; }
  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    text-transform: none; color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .eyebrow::before { content: '> '; white-space: pre; opacity: 0.55; font-weight: 700; }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--text-primary); margin: 0.5rem 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .updated { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 1.75rem; }
  .intro { font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  ul { margin: 0 0 1rem 1.2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  li { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
  strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .disclaimer {
    margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
